<title>USA: Vivus seeks Swedish OK of impotence drug.</title>
<headline>Vivus seeks Swedish OK of impotence drug.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vivus Inc said it applied for approval in Sweden to market its MUSE urethral suppository to treat impotence.</p>
<p>The company filed for approval in the U.K. in September, and in the United States in March. Vivus said earlier this month it received U.S. Food and Drug Administration approvable status for Muse as a treatment for impotence.</p>
<p>MUSE is a small, single-use, disposable applicator containing alprostadil, a synthetic version of a naturally occurring substance, vasoldilator prostaglandin E1.</p>
</text>
